Domain-Specific Guidance

The Central Theme is an orientation layer.

It is not an interpretation layer.

Enterprise Characteristics

The Central Theme shall be:

Brief
Human-centered
Conversational
Context-aware
Domain-neutral
Architecturally reusable
Independent of any individual knowledge domain
Domain Implementation Examples
Bible Therapy Assistant (BTA)

User

My grandson passed away and I am depressed.

Central Theme

God's Word speaks hope to grieving hearts.

Authoritative Knowledge

Scripture

OSHA Assistant

User

Do I need fall protection on this roof?

Central Theme

Fall protection requirements depend on the work being performed.

Authoritative Knowledge

OSHA Regulations

Healthcare Assistant

User

My blood sugar keeps rising after dinner.

Central Theme

Several factors can influence evening blood sugar levels.

Authoritative Knowledge

Clinical guidance and approved medical references

Legal Assistant

User

Can my employer terminate me without notice?

Central Theme

Employment rights depend upon applicable laws and circumstances.

Authoritative Knowledge

Statutes, regulations, and case law

Governance

The Central Theme shall derive its context from the governed intent analysis process and shall remain subordinate to the domain's authoritative knowledge.

Implementations may customize wording and tone appropriate to their domain but shall not alter the constitutional purpose of the Central Theme Layer.

Authority

This Enterprise Principle defines a reusable HCGO semantic interaction pattern.

Individual implementations (such as Bible Therapy Assistant, OSHA Assistant, Healthcare Assistant, and future HCGO solutions) shall implement this principle in accordance with their respective domain authorities.

I would make one final naming change. Since this is an Enterprise Principle, I'd remove the RTL prefix altogether and use:

EP-001 — Central Theme Layer

Then, within BTA Version 5.6, you would reference it as:

Implementation of HCGO EP-001 — Central Theme Layer

That keeps the enterprise architecture clean: the principle belongs to HCGO, while BTA, OSHA, Healthcare, and other domains simply implement it according to their authoritative knowledge source.
